# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Dustfile — Cleanup and hygiene contract for boj-server-cartridges
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>
#
# Paired runner: dust.ncl
# Verb:          dust
# Semantics:     What should be cleaned up. Housekeeping, not blockers.
#
# Rewritten 2026-08-07. The previous version had this repository's name
# substituted in but still described it as "the canonical template" whose
# cleanup items "ensure the template itself remains pristine", and several of
# its checks pointed at paths that do not exist here.

[metadata]
project = "boj-server-cartridges"
version = "0.2.0"
last-updated = "2026-08-07"

@abstract:
Cleanup and hygiene items for boj-server-cartridges. Housekeeping only —
nothing here blocks a merge. Every check below was run on 2026-08-07; the
`measured` line records what it returned rather than what it should return.
@end

## Build Output

### no-build-artifacts-tracked
- description: No .zig-cache, zig-out or compiled objects tracked in git
- run: test -z "$(git ls-files | grep -E 'zig-cache|zig-out|\.(so|o|a)$')"
- measured: passes (2026-08-07)
- severity: warning
- notes: The working tree DOES accumulate .zig-cache and .so files from local builds. They are gitignored, which is correct, but they make `grep -r` and `find` over cartridges/ slow enough to time out. Prefer `git grep` and `git ls-files` in any check that scans the tree.

### no-stray-scratch-files
- description: No scratch or test-run leftovers at the repository root
- run: test -z "$(ls template-test-* tmp-* scratch-* 2>/dev/null)"
- measured: passes (2026-08-07)
- severity: info

## Contractile Hygiene

### no-example-placeholder-files
- description: No EXAMPLE- or SAMPLE- files in contractiles/
- run: test -z "$(find .machine_readable/contractiles/ -name 'EXAMPLE-*' -o -name 'SAMPLE-*')"
- measured: passes — 0 found (2026-08-07)
- severity: warning

### no-old-contractile-formats
- description: No legacy .contractile or .hs files remaining
- run: test -z "$(find .machine_readable/contractiles/ \( -name '*.contractile' -o -name '*.hs' \))"
- measured: passes — 0 found (2026-08-07)
- severity: warning

### contractile-runners-exist
- description: Each contractile names a paired .ncl runner in its header; those runners should exist
- run: test -n "$(find .machine_readable/contractiles -name '*.ncl' -print -quit)"
- measured: FAILS — 0 .ncl files exist anywhere in this repository (2026-08-07)
- severity: info
- notes: All six contractiles declare a paired runner (intend.ncl, must.ncl, trust.ncl, adjust.ncl, bust.ncl, dust.ncl). None exists. Either generate them or stop naming them. Recorded here rather than in Mustfile because the checks are perfectly runnable as plain shell without a runner — the absence is untidy, not broken.

### contractiles-justfile-is-not-a-link
- description: The RSR convention hardlinks the root Justfile to .machine_readable/contractiles/Justfile
- run: test "$(stat -c '%i' Justfile)" = "$(stat -c '%i' .machine_readable/contractiles/Justfile)"
- measured: FAILS — different inodes AND different content (2026-08-07)
- severity: info
- notes: .machine_readable/contractiles/Justfile is still rsr-template-repo's template Justfile — it declares project := "rsr-template-repo" and version := "0.1.0", and its recipes do not match this repo's. Decide whether it is meant to be a hardlink to the root Justfile or an independently maintained template copy, then make it one of those two. Deliberately left alone by the docs/machine-readable-repair branch, which touched only .a2ml files.

## Documentation Hygiene

### no-general-md-in-docs
- description: docs/ should be AsciiDoc; .md is reserved for the files GitHub special-cases by name
- run: test -z "$(find docs -name '*.md')"
- measured: FAILS — 1 file: docs/echo-types-integration-audit-2026-06-01.md (2026-08-07)
- severity: info

### no-stale-counts-in-readme
- description: README.adoc should not assert a manifest count the validator disagrees with
- run: grep -q '142' README.adoc
- measured: FAILS — README.adoc still says "139 manifests, 139 passing, 0 failing" (lines 25, 118, 132); the validator reports 142/142/0 (2026-08-07)
- severity: warning
- notes: Left for a separate change so the README correction is not buried inside the machine-readable repair.

### no-duplicate-readme-format
- description: Only one README format in contractiles/ (.adoc canonical)
- run: test ! -f .machine_readable/contractiles/README.md
- measured: passes (2026-08-07)
- severity: info

## Repository Hygiene

### no-untracked-workflows
- description: Every file in .github/workflows/ should be tracked in git
- run: test -z "$(git ls-files -o --exclude-standard .github/workflows/)"
- measured: FAILS — .github/workflows/main-estate-audit.yml is untracked (2026-08-07)
- severity: warning
- notes: It calls 26 hyperpolymath/cicd-suite actions, all pinned to @main rather than a SHA. Commit it with SHA pins or delete it. Leaving it untracked means it neither runs nor gets reviewed.

### no-broken-symlinks
- description: No broken symbolic links
- run: test -z "$(find . -path ./.git -prune -o -xtype l -print)"
- measured: passes — 0 found (2026-08-07)
- severity: info
